videos.script:
Lesson 7 drew the planner as one screen. A real app has several, and a way back between them that the platform owns. {{screens}}

Today the planner gets two screens: the courses, and one course with its sessions and a form. {{two}} You will meet the six components almost every screen is made of, and the one rule about text that every web developer breaks once. {{text}}

Then styles, which look like CSS and are not. {{styles}} There is no cascade, the layout is flexbox only, and it stacks downwards by default.

Navigation comes from files. {{files}} Every file in the app folder is a screen, and its path is its address.

And accessibility, on both sides. {{axe}} You will run axe over the web build, see it pass, and then see it fail on one colour.
